implementation, in any language, under any licence, with no obligation.

Nothing in this directory is code and nothing in it is prose about kindkit. It
describes the shape of a conformance case tree and nothing else, so that a tree
can be consumed without reading Python and without inheriting a licence.

Embedding conformance cases — or the rules describing them — inside a
share-alike specification document is the CommonMark mistake this split exists
to avoid.

The full text is at https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
and, in the kindkit repository this directory came from, in LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt.
A relative path is deliberately not used: this directory is meant to be copied
out on its own, and a link that dangles in the vendored copy is worse than none.
